KZ3 patch 2042 (RSX pass 42): PSO keys and HLSL depend only on the texture units the fragment program samples.
rsx_fp_decompiler.c/.h: rsx_fp_texture_unit_mask(ucode, size) = units of TEX/TXP/TXD/TXL/TXB.
rsx_live_draw.c: the per-unit loops that build cube/gamma/shadow/ARGB-alias masks and the unnormalised-size table
skip units the program does not sample. State left bound on unused units made new PSO keys and new HLSL (one level
session: 1,281 PSOs from 248 fragment programs, 78 distinct cube masks, 139 gamma masks, 869 pixel-shader
sources), so the pso_keys.bin / shader blobs of an earlier session rarely matched (release pass 17: 54 of 4,933
keys used, 897 compiles). LD_PSO_ALL_UNITS=1 restores the old key; pso_keys.bin version 2 (old files restart).
Diagnostics: LD_PSO_KEYLOG=<file> (one line per PSO built: key components, HLSL hashes); LD_GAMMA_ORDER=rgb|argb
(which channels TEXTURE_ADDRESS gamma bits decode; rgb = patch 2009, default). Log: [pso-key], [gamma] order.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): context only.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

